Concurrency Control Manager (CCM)

Class diagram: docs/ccm-class-diagram.drawio (PNG export next to it).
Contract: IConcurrencyControlManager and IFailureRecoveryManager follow the SQLike supergroup report (section 2.1).

Milestone 1 status
- Every IConcurrencyControlManager method is callable through sqlike.ccm.ConcurrencyControlManager,
  so QP and FRM can integrate against it now.
- Parts that are still mocks are marked TODO(CCx), where CCx is the role that implements them.

Packages (src/main/java)
- sqlike.contract  IConcurrencyControlManager (CCM) and IFailureRecoveryManager (FRM), copied from the contract
- sqlike.shared    shared data types copied from the contract; delete once a supergroup shared package exists
- sqlike.ccm       CCM classes:
    ConcurrencyControlManager, CCMConfig, TransactionManager, Transaction   transactions and protocol choice (CC-01, CC-02)
    FRMBridge                                                                WAL logging, abort, recovery (CC-03, CC-04, CC-05)
    IConcurrencyProtocol, LockBasedProtocol                                  lock-based access (CC-06)
    DeadlockHandler                                                          deadlock handling (CC-07)
    TimestampProtocol                                                        timestamp-based access (CC-08)
    ScheduleOperation, ScheduleRecorder, SerializabilityVerifier             serializability check (CC-09)
    CCMDriver, Scenario, MockFRM                                             standalone driver (CC-10)

Build and run the driver (JDK 17 or newer), from the repository root:
  javac --release 17 -d out $(find concurrency-control/src/main/java -name '*.java')
  java -cp out sqlike.ccm.CCMDriver
The driver runs every scenario against ConcurrencyControlManager with MockFRM and prints
"Total: N/N skenario LULUS" when all of them pass.
